data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":1104,"item_id":"fc_0d5196a05473f4b0016adb3557573081918e1a9ff5a498ea63","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"artifact_json\":\"{\\\"inference\\\":\\\"R001\\\",\\\"packet_sha256\\\":\\\"f137aaa18381ba1dcbccb617b121d1d21e96727a95a2b8dc5ebdfd8f353ac2b4\\\",\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"FAIL\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"Fresh packet-only mathematical review of the complete packet, with declared Yui Audit A/self-containment/format rules as procedure only. No source proof or other mathematical material was consulted. First defect: S005 uses e_i as vectors of M tensor_Z K, but e_i was declared in the complex V(lambda); S004 instead describes the reduced basis as images of a e_i, also named b_i. S005 does not identify its e_i with those images. Therefore the expansion of w and the conclusion that all basis vectors belong to W are not established as written. I do not repair the argument. Input boundary: packet.json read in full and the declared rules. No runtime-attestation claim; carrier identity, canonical hash binding and transmitted-material readback are outside this review.\\\",\\\"checks\\\":{\\\"inputs\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"H001-H004 are the stated direct inputs, and the argument uses no outside premise.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inputs/0\\\",\\\"/inputs/1\\\",\\\"/inputs/2\\\",\\\"/inputs/3\\\",\\\"/inference/inputs\\\"]},\\\"argument\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"FAIL\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"The first unsupported step is S005's expansion in e_i and the ensuing matrix-unit conclusion: the proof needs a basis of the K-module, while the declared e_i are complex vectors and the reduced images are separately named/described.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/argument/3/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/4/text\\\",\\\"/inference/locals/2\\\",\\\"/inference/locals/14\\\"]},\\\"dependency_accounting\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"FAIL\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"S005 relies on identifying its e_i with the reduced/scalar-extended basis. Although S004 describes that basis and b_i is declared, S005 does not use or state that identification in the critical calculation.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/argument/3/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/4/text\\\",\\\"/inference/locals/14\\\"]},\\\"output\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"UNVERIFIED\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"S005 purports to prove nonzeroness and the invariant-subspace criterion, but the basis argument needed for irreducibility is not closed.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/output/statement\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/4/text\\\"]},\\\"scope\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"W is introduced as an arbitrary invariant subspace; no temporary assumption or witness escapes. The defect is the basis-object mismatch.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/locals/12\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/4/text\\\"]},\\\"applicability\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"No E/M inputs or source applications occur; H inputs are the only premises.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/inputs\\\",\\\"/inference/applications\\\"]},\\\"statement_closure\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"The full input and target statements, including the nonzero and invariant-subspace content, are present in the packet. This does not establish the proof.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inputs/0/statement\\\",\\\"/inputs/1/statement\\\",\\\"/inputs/2/statement\\\",\\\"/inputs/3/statement\\\",\\\"/output/statement\\\"]},\\\"object_closure\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"FAIL\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"S005 uses e_i as K-module vectors, whereas the local declaration defines e_i in V(lambda) over C. The reduced images are described in S004 and declared as b_i, but S005 does not identify its occurrences with those objects.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/locals/2\\\",\\\"/inference/locals/14\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/3/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/4/text\\\"]},\\\"dependency_closure\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"FAIL\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"The decisive implication that every basis vector is in W depends on an unestablished identification of the e_i in S005 with the reduced/scalar-extended basis.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/argument/3/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/4/text\\\",\\\"/inference/locals/14\\\"]},\\\"packet_replay\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"FAIL\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"From this packet alone the argument is insufficient as written at S005 for the identified basis-object gap. No source or other inference proof was used. Replay judgment does not authenticate carrier identity, hash binding or readback.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/argument/4/text\\\",\\\"/inference/locals/2\\\",\\\"/inference/locals/14\\\"]}},\\\"findings\\\":[{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"FAIL\\\",\\\"location\\\":\\\"/inference/argument/4/text\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The step w=sum_i c_i e_i and E_j,i w=c_i e_j requires e_i to denote basis vectors in M tensor_Z K. e_i is declared as a complex vector in V(lambda); the reduced/scalar-extended images are separately identified as a e_i/b_i in S004 and the locals. No identification is stated in S005, so this implication is not established within the packet.\\\"}]}\"}"}

